  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 VDocs – Release Notes\n\t\t🚀 Version: 2026.11.1\n        \n        This release turns the VDocs façade into a fully IDisposable, stream‑friendly, and async‑capable entry point, adds convenient byte‑array helpers, and introduces two new AddParagraph overloads. It also renames the HTML service types to align with the naming convention used across the rest of the library.\n\nExisting code keeps compiling thanks to [Obsolete] aliases for GetHTML and SaveAsHTML. New code should prefer the new names.\n\n✨ Added\nNew constructors and factory methods for streams\n\n - VDocs(Stream input) — open an existing .docx directly from a Stream. The caller keeps ownership of the stream; it is not closed or disposed.\n\n - VDocs.OpenFromWord(Stream input) — fluent equivalent of the new stream constructor.\n\n - VDocs.OpenFromWordAsync(Stream input, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) — reads the stream asynchronously into a buffer, then parses synchronously (parsing is CPU-bound). Fully cancellable.\n\n - VDocs.OpenFromPdf(Stream input), VDocs.OpenFromPdfAsync(…) — placeholders that throw NotImplementedException (PDF import still pending).\n\n - VDocs.OpenFromHtml(Stream input), VDocs.OpenFromHtmlAsync(…) — placeholders that throw NotImplementedException (HTML import still pending).\n\n\nNew save methods and overloads\n\n - SaveAsWord(Stream output), SaveAsHtml(Stream output), SaveAsPdf(Stream output) — write the rendered document to any writable stream. The stream is left open, so callers can chain multiple operations.\n\n - SaveAsWordAsync(Stream output, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default), SaveAsHtmlAsync(…), SaveAsPdfAsync(…) — the render happens synchronously into an internal buffer, and the write to the caller's stream is awaited. The stream is left open and the operation is cancellable.\n\n - ToWordBytes() — renders the document to .docx and returns the raw byte[].\n\n - ToPdfBytes() — renders the document to PDF and returns the raw byte[]. Useful for embedding in JSON payloads, emails, or blob uploads without touching the file system.\n\nNew AddParagraph overloads\n\n - AddParagraph(string text) — creates a paragraph that contains a single Text run with the given content.\n\n - AddParagraph(params IText[] runs) — creates a paragraph composed of the supplied runs in order. Useful for building inline formatted content (bold label + value + suffix) without manually calling AddText multiple times.\n\nIDisposable support\n\n - VDocs now implements IDisposable.\n\n - Dispose() — releases the pooled package part streams owned by the document. Calling it more than once is safe.\n\n - protected virtual Dispose(bool disposing) — the standard .NET disposal pattern, so derived test doubles or wrappers can extend cleanup.\n\n - ThrowIfDisposed() — internal guard that throws ObjectDisposedException from GetHtml, SaveAs*, SaveAs*Async, ToWordBytes, and ToPdfBytes when the instance has already been disposed. This makes use-after-free bugs surface immediately instead of silently corrupting state.\n\nAutomatic theme activation\n\n - All three constructors now auto-activate the first theme found in the document’s DocumentStyles.Themes collection. This matches what Word does when it opens a document — the theme the file was saved with is now the active theme without any additional API calls from the caller. If no theme is present, the constructor does nothing and the document remains on its default styling.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
